    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Finding the equation of a line"
    },
    {
      "type": "formula",
      "latex": "a = \\frac{y_2 - y_1}{x_2 - x_1}",
      "caption": "Gradient between two points"
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 2",
      "problem": "Find the equation of the line through $(1; 5)$ and $(3; 9)$.",
      "steps": [
        "$a = \\dfrac{9 - 5}{3 - 1} = 2$, so $y = 2x + q$.",
        "Substitute $(1; 5)$: $5 = 2(1) + q$, so $q = 3$.",
        "$y = 2x + 3$"
      ],
      "answer": "$y = 2x + 3$"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Domain, range and interpretation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "For $y = ax + q$ with $a \\neq 0$, the domain and range are both all real numbers: $x \\in \\mathbb{R}$ and $y \\in \\mathbb{R}$. If $a = 0$, the range is just $\\{q\\}$. In real-life problems the domain is often restricted, e.g. time cannot be negative."
    },
    {
      "type": "example",
      "title": "Worked example 3: a real-life line",
      "problem": "A plumber charges a call-out fee of R250 plus R180 per hour. Write a formula for the cost $C$ of a job lasting $h$ hours and find the cost of a 3-hour job.",
      "steps": [
        "$C = 180h + 250$: gradient R180 per hour, $C$-intercept R250.",
        "$C = 180(3) + 250 = 790$"
      ],
      "answer": "R790"
    }
